# Contract and schema JSON are byte-compared, not merely parsed: the
# contract-distribution suite asserts that the files on disk are the canonical
# bytes of the embedded registry dicts (agent-platform/routing/schema_source.py,
# scripts/export_contracts.py). Canonical form is LF.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true -- the default on Windows and the setting in use on
# the maintainer's machine -- git rewrites those LFs to CRLF on checkout, and
# every freshly created worktree then fails the comparison against bytes that
# are correct in the repository. This was diagnosed and repaired by hand twice
# during the W-series, once per worktree, without the cause being addressed.
#
# Pinning the eol here fixes it at the source: the blobs are already LF, and
# checkout no longer rewrites them.
contracts/**/*.json text eol=lf
schemas/**/*.json   text eol=lf
